WEBVTT

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.970
One, two, three, four!

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:34.970
One, two, three, four!

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.720
One, two, three, four!

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.700
One, two, three, four!

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.480
Done!

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.110
Good! You were perfectly in sync.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.860
Landing your final pose might be easier 
if you start your jump sooner.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.640
Don't force it too much, though.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.570
Okay!

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.380
Oh, just in time...

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.020
That's it for today!

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.350
Okay!

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.720
The new routine is pretty hard, huh?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.590
I always forget if I should use 
my left hand or my right!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.110
Yeah, same here.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.420
So this... turns into this.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.590
I know!

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.620
It's really nice when it comes 
together, though.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.980
Let's practice it a lot!

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.130
Yeah.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.860
<i>Kero-chan stayed home</i>

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.330
<i>because there was an event in his online 
game he didn't want to miss.</i>

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.600
<i>So I won't have to worry about 
him talking in his sleep.</i>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.310
Ya can't put eel and pickled plum 
together! Whose idea was that?

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.850
<i>He's pretty loud, so it always makes 
me nervous during class.</i>

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.690
What's wrong?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.740
I just got a message...

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:50.140
<b>Sakura and Welcome Back, Meiling</b>

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.010
Over here.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.510
Heya!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.540
Meiling-chan!

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.090
It's the real you!

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.700
Is there a fake me?

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.670
No, no!

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.070
You've sent pictures and appeared 
in my dreams a few times,

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.420
but this is the real you!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.670
You'll have to tell me about 
these dreams later.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.250
There she is! Over there!

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.490
Wow, it's really Meiling-chan!

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.110
Meiling-chan!

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.970
Have you all been well?

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:21.840
Yeah!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.750
We've been great!

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.440
And have you been well, Meiling-chan?

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.220
Just see for yourself!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.350
Is this the new friend I've heard about?

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.920
Yeah! That's Akiho Shinomoto-chan!

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.860
I'm Akiho. It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:38.180
I'm Meiling Lin, Syaoran's cousin.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.160
Yes, Sakura-san has told me about you.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.740
Why so formal? You sound like Daidouji-san.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:48.580
Before coming to Japan, Akiho-chan 
lived in several other countries.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.990
So this is the kind of Japanese she learned.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.240
Really? Well, it's nice to 
meet you, Shinomoto-san.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.250
Likewise.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.510
But what brings you here, all of a sudden?

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.300
I told you I was coming 
to Japan soon, didn't I?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.230
You did, but I thought it'd be later, 
like over summer break.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.260
Surprised?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.530
Super surprised.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.270
Then, I was successful!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.270
Meiling!

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.650
Néih hóu ma, Syaoran?

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.120
You didn't tell me you were coming.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.370
Surprised?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.760
Obviously!

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.610
Then, I was successful!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.880
Meiling!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.470
I'm sure you two have a lot to 
talk about, after so long,

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:29.490
but we could get in trouble for hanging 
around the gate too long.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.900
R-Right...

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.910
Speaking of gates, try not 
to take <i>a fence</i>, but—

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:40.490
Don't drag this out any longer, 
after saying we shouldn't!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:42.420
<b>That's a pun</b>

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:47.420
Chiharu-chan and Naoko-chan seemed 
sad they couldn't talk to you more.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.250
Well, I'll be here for a few days.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.160
Besides, isn't tomorrow a day off?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:51.930
Yeah!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.940
We'll have to go shopping, first.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.640
I only have enough food for one at home.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.220
That's fine, isn't it? You live on your own.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.290
Are you on a diet again or something?

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.110
Wh-What?

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.370
<b>Diet</b>

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.370
I was just a little surprised to hear 
the word "diet" coming from you.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.640
Th-That's not what I meant!

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.080
Meiling was always saying that she'd 
diet while she was in Hong Kong!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.630
N-No, really... I-It just 
surprised me a little.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.530
Uh, I shouldn't be surprised 
by that, huh? Sorry.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:25.630
No, it's...

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.220
I-It's nothing you need to apologize for.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.910
S-Still, I'm sorry.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.510
Okay, that's enough.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:35.180
I'm done with my diet. The reason 
you won't need food for me is...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.380
Kinomoto-san?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:36.890
Yes?

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.650
Let me stay with you, okay?

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.010
Huh?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.880
I did it! Man, these event-only 
bosses sure are tough!

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.290
That would've been a little easier 
if Spinny'd been around...

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.440
I'm home!

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:02.260
Well, she sounds awful happy.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.590
I'm home, Kero-chan!

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.130
Hey, welcome home!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:07.890
Boo!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.810
You still look like a stuffed toy.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.120
Huh...

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.920
So that's why you're here.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.000
Yep.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.230
This is good.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.440
I made it just the way you taught me.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.510
It was Wei who taught it to me.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.860
Syaoran-kun told me 
Wei-san's doing really well.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.600
He sure is.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.830
But he's really worried about Syaoran 
being in Japan, all by himself.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:39.430
"Is he eating enough vegetables?"

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.960
"I hope he keeps his belly 
covered when he sleeps."

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:44.380
He's like that every day.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:45.850
H-His belly...

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:50.080
I guess Syaoran will always 
be a baby in Wei's mind.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.350
<b>Dad</b>

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:56.340
It's my dad.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.190
Hello, this is Sakura.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.110
Yeah, I'm at home with Meiling-chan now.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:09.930
Let me talk.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:14.160
Mind if I let Meiling-chan talk to you?

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.440
Hello, I'm Meiling Lin.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.960
I'm very sorry for asking to 
stay on such short notice.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.850
Yes, it's all right.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.450
I've spoken to my parents in Hong Kong.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.590
Yes. I'll do my best not to cause 
trouble for all of you.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.960
Oh, no, she was a good friend 
when I lived in Japan before.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.340
Yes, sir. Thank you so much. 
I appreciate the hospitality.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.120
Okay, I'll give the phone 
back to Sakura-san now.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.220
This is Sakura.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.500
Yeah, we'll be fine on our own.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.490
Dad, don't work too hard, okay?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.390
Bye.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.620
Meiling-chan, you sound so 
grown-up on the phone!

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.980
It's just good manners. 
Besides, he's letting me stay here.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.670
I have to be careful not to worry him.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.930
So you were trying to act even
more innocent than usual.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.590
What did you say?!

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.200
Hey, look! Cookies.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.970
They're really good!

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.340
Oh, you're right.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.810
Akiho-chan gave them to me.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.930
Kaito-san made them.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.710
He's the guy who's sort of like Wei, right?

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:38.100
Yeah, he's a butler who 
looks after Akiho-chan

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.380
and does lots of things for her.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.070
A butler...

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.690
You're not wrong, but coming from you,

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.580
it sounds more like the fluffy animal.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.810
Yeah, I get that.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:51.810
<b>Baa</b>

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:56.050
Still, even with a butler,

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.730
living alone in Japan, in middle 
school, would be hard.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.870
Yeah, it must be.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.180
I guess Syaoran's doing it, too, but...

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.750
Yeah.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.010
I wish there were something 
I could do to help him...

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.180
I think you're doing plenty!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:16.480
Just staying close to him and 
laughing a lot should be enough!

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.190
But...

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.920
Well, I guess there are some things 
you don't always realize for yourself.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.590
True.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.190
Anyway, where's your brother?

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.880
I'd like to say hello.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.240
He's staying at Yukito-san's place, tonight.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.670
They have exams comin' up, right?

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:33.820
Yeah.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.340
I hope he's not being too 
demanding of Yukito-san...

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.620
You okay? Want to go inside?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.760
Nah.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.340
Catching a cold? I have medicine.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:49.230
No, someone's talking trash about me.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:49.950
Huh?

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.120
And it's a monster doing it.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.990
You're always talking about 
Sakura-chan like that.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.150
She sent me a message earlier.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:05.780
Said a friend of hers, who moved 
away, is back in Japan

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:07.000
and staying at our place.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.930
Is it Meiling-chan?

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:09.490
Yeah.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.500
Sakura-chan must be so happy!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:15.130
The emoji in her message 
definitely looked thrilled.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.090
Fujitaka-san isn't home today, either, is he?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.640
So it's just Sakura-chan and Meiling-chan?

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:24.260
Toya, are you sure you shouldn't go home?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.770
Dad said it's fine, so it's fine.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.530
That's... kinda nice.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:32.760
What is?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.920
I'm not sure how to put it...

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.270
The way you all trust each other, I guess.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:45.530
Toya...

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:51.800
At work a while ago, you said now, 
you could do something new.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.800
You still won't tell me what it is?

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.390
You said I'd find out when it was time.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.100
Do you know when that will be?

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.810
I don't know when it'll happen,

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:12.820
but when it does, you'll know.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:43.650
Your power is slowly returning.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.650
You no longer have the power you 
gave me to maintain this form.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.880
But so long as you live,

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:58.420
you think it's possible that a new power 
could gradually grow within you?

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.890
I don't really get it myself.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.240
And the master?

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:04.830
She hasn't noticed.

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:09.610
Of course, she didn't notice when 
I had the power before, either.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.620
Why won't you tell me about this new power?

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:16.040
This isn't the time to tell you.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:17.870
That's all.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.690
Once you've made up your
mind, you won't change it.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:27.880
Just like your sister.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:29.890
I'll change back.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.890
Study well for these exams of yours.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:45.650
Oh? Did I change again?

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:04.880
Huh? With a knife?

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.930
In Hong Kong, we'd use a 
spatula to make gyoza,

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.050
but if you don't have one, 
a butter knife works.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.270
I would've liked to make the shells, too,

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.680
but we'll use store-bought ones, today.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.690
I ate them a lot when I was in Japan before.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.400
The shells they sell here are 
really good, aren't they?

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:24.930
Yeah!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.810
Why can't you use a spoon, though?

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.700
It traps air bubbles in the filling.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.320
Then, they puff up, when fried, 
and lose flavor.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:36.830
Wow!

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:41.020
It's the same when you wrap them. 
Try not to trap air inside.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:44.080
O-Okay. I'm kinda nervous...

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.710
Get some filling,

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:49.390
make sure not to trap air inside...

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:01.820
Even if it's a little misshapen, 
it's fine, as long as it's tightly sealed.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.770
How's it going?

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.660
Great!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.280
Perilla goes in this one, right?

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.540
Yep.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:11.530
In our family, we make regular gyoza 
and another type with perilla.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.540
I can't wait to try it!

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.540
Oh, also, I steam them before I fry them.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.040
We do, too!

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.680
I'll leave the frying to you, then.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.200
I'll make the soup.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.220
Okay!

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:26.290
I'll cheer ya on!

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.930
That's what you do most 
of the time, Kero-chan.

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:31.430
Reassuring, ain't it?

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.420
They look so good!

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:38.930
Let's eat!

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.920
Yum!

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:52.530
They're so good!

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.160
I guess even you have somethin' 
you're good at, huh, brat?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.400
What did you say?!

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.880
It was a compliment...

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.480
It didn't sound like one!

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.810
Well, bein' hungry makes people cranky.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.260
Here, have some gyoza.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.190
That still doesn't sound like a compliment!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.680
They really are good!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.210
You're amazing, Meiling-chan!

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:16.760
B-Being complimented so openly 
is a little unsettling...

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:21.280
I guess that means no one normally 
gives ya compliments!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.580
None for you.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.370
What's the big idea?!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.760
Grr!

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.510
One more... Just one more...

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.620
Yum, yum...

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:40.000
The perilla's good, but make some 
cheese gyoza, next time.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.780
So carefree for a Creature of the Seal.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.000
You're not being a bother, are you?

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.670
Nothing weird has happened, has it?

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.780
He worries too much.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:00.650
Everything's fine.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:03.760
Have Kinomoto-san make you gyoza, sometime.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.130
Well, Kinomoto-san hasn't changed at all...

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.650
I guess I can't blame him for worrying.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.040
That was a quick bath!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.530
Huh? Yeah.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.410
You didn't dry your hair?

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:25.290
I have a dryer in here. Plus...

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:30.050
I wanted to get back sooner, 
to talk with you.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:36.010
Natural airheads are such a hassle, really.

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:38.790
Give me that.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:45.340
You really don't mind?

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:48.510
I've always wanted to try 
drying someone else's hair.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.030
Your long hair must be pretty hard to dry.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:54.300
Yeah, but I'm used to it.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.740
Tomoyo-chan said it's hard for her, too.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:03.040
So she said her mom invented a hair 
dryer for long hair, just for her.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.550
I know!

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:08.370
She sent one over to me, in Hong Kong.

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:11.460
L-Leave it to Tomoyo-chan...

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.880
There, it's dry.

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:15.560
Thanks.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.010
It looks good that way, too.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.130
Do you ever think of growing it out?

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.640
I like the idea of it,

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.100
but it seems like it'd be hard 
to manage in the morning.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.150
Syaoran doesn't have any particular 
hairstyle preferences, you know.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:38.640
In fact, he never showed any 
interest in girls in Hong Kong.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.610
I wonder if Syaoran-kun...

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.620
is lonely, with all of his 
family in Hong Kong.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:51.370
Last time, he had you and Wei-san,

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.330
but he's really on his own now.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:59.410
Last time, he came here for the Clow Cards.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.130
And he stayed because another thing came up.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:05.610
The "Sakura Cards," was it?

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:09.130
He returned to Hong Kong, saying the 
cards had changed into them.

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:14.160
But the whole time he was there, 
he kept saying he'd go back to Japan...

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:23.920
I thought it would take longer, though.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:27.640
Syaoran's mother is the head 
of the Li family now,

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.030
and after her, he's the strongest of us.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.540
I'm sure there's a lot he needs to learn 
to be the next family head

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:37.970
and a lot of things he'll have to remember.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.540
Some of his relatives tried to stop 
him from going to Japan.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.690
But he came to Japan, anyway.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:48.800
In the end, he got permission from 
my aunt, the current head.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:52.190
It's probably because he wanted to see you.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.010
You're not happy about that?

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.830
If that's true, I am.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:06.320
But ever since Syaoran-kun came back, 
he's had something on his mind.

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:10.140
Something important that he can't tell me.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:15.490
So I wondered if, even when he's smiling, 
he's actually hurting, somehow...

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:18.590
Did Syaoran tell you that?

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.810
I haven't asked him anything.

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:26.490
I feel like I can't ask.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:27.610
Why?

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:29.720
I don't know.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:34.740
But if it's something he can 
tell me, I think he will.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:40.000
I'm sure it would be stressful for him to 
tell me something he didn't want to.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:49.100
It's hard when you're both too 
important to each other.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.720
What?

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:53.880
I said, so what will you do, then?

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:00.240
I want to do whatever I can on my own,

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:03.120
so he won't have more to worry about!

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:06.870
That's right.

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:12.030
I'm sure the most important thing 
to him is that you keep smiling!

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.260
Thanks!

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:21.770
Huh? Meiling-chan, did you bring 
those from Hong Kong?

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:22.670
Huh?

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.300
The cat ears.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.340
Cat?

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:28.070
And you're wearing a tail?

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.080
What are you talking about?

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.740
It's moving a lot!

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:32.570
Are you half-asleep?

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:36.150
I don't think so...

00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:37.380
Huh?

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:38.740
Huh?

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:40.420
What?

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:42.970
You really are half-asleep.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.050
We're meeting up with everyone, tomorrow,

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.600
so let's get to bed!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:48.340
O-Okay.

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:49.840
Thanks.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:53.030
You're sure you're okay with the futon?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:56.960
Yeah. It's been ages since 
I slept on a futon!

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:00.840
What?

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:03.990
N-Nothing! Let's get some sleep!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.870
Goodnight, Kinomoto-san.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.680
Night, Meiling-chan.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.150
What?

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.150
No, it's nothing.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:29.340
Night.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:34.120
Night.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.610
Yes, come in.

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.620
This is chamomile tea. Would you like some?

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:50.620
Yes, please!

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:59.090
Reading that book again?

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:03.400
I can read more of the parts I 
couldn't understand before.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:05.290
And what is it about?

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:09.100
A girl who grows a cat's ears and tail.

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:14.600
Alice finds out and tries to tell everyone,

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.590
but they instantly disappear.

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:18.600
I see.

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:21.610
I look forward to hearing 
the rest of that story.

00:24:10.060 --> 00:24:12.370
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.630
Yo! It's "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.350
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.350
<b>K</b>

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:18.790
Today, we're lookin' at 
Tomoyo's recording devices!

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:21.510
Of course, she's always carryin' 
these camcorders around.

00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:22.770
She records with a smartphone, too.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:25.270
And with the drone, filming 
from the air is a snap.

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:29.080
And above all, there's this, the super-cool 
action camera I wear on my head!

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:32.190
Daidouji Toys developed it due 
to Tomoyo's sheer tenacity!

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:33.850
Man, I look so cool!

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:33.850 --> 00:24:36.380
Ah, there's so much more 
I wanna introduce to ya!

00:24:36.380 --> 00:24:37.820
Give me a longer time slot!

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:39.710
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.750
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.750
Meiling-chan and I are meeting 
everyone at the shrine to hang out.

00:24:43.160 --> 00:24:45.360
What? Ears? A tail?

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:48.700
Huh?! Meiling-chan really turned into a cat!

00:24:49.090 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura, the Shrine, and the Zoo</b>

00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:52.090
Next time, "Sakura, the Shrine, and the Zoo."

00:24:52.090 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:57.470
<b>End</b>
